 reach out to people around you and  you know explore  any potential future projects that you  could work on together because  everyone has a unique expertise so by  working together you can achieve greater  things so i think that there are things  that i could say related to coursework  or to you know  the intellectual inquiry that you'll do  and how to think about research but i  think what maybe is more important than  any of that to your long-term success in  the program  is  finding a group of people that you  resonate with and i think sometimes  people come in  to the program and they kind of get in a  local minima where they're surrounded by  a certain type of people and they think  that this is true for the rest of the  community and that's not the case and  you can find people that will  you know resonate with you and make you  feel like you're growing and learning in  the right ways and make you feel like  you belong and so if you're interacting  with people that don't make you feel  like you belong  there's someone else that you can work  with i think it's really really  important that you know how to take care  of yourself so if you come to mit you  need to find a support network and you  need to rely on those people because  it's going to be hard if you come here  that's the nature of the work that we're  doing and it's the nature of the  institute and so finding those friends  finding those people you can rely on uh  that will get you through  it's cold  but you can deal with it you know it  takes a little bit of suffering  tolerance  [Music]

